  "phase_boundaries": "Boundaries are file-open landmarks, not function boundaries: 1 first execve -> beam.smp execve; 2 beam exec -> init_debug `started`; 3 `started` -> first open of Elixir.BeamLisp.Application.beam; 4 -> first open of Ns.Vm.Native; 5 -> first open of Ns.Release; 6 -> first open of Ns.Bl.Cli; 7 -> open of the user file; 8 -> last traced open (the program runs here). Exit adds about 25 ms (timed runs, user form to process exit).",
  "not_measured": "Per-function time inside phases 4 and 5 cannot be had without an SDK edit or a profiler attached inside the VM. perf is not installed; Elixir Logger removes the OTP default handler when the :logger app starts, so application_controller progress reports after elixir were not obtainable (two attempts, kept in the journal). The cause of the full-tree sweeps is read from source (aot.bl sdk_runtime_inventory_uncached!, env.bl retain_sdk_runtime!), not from a trace.",
  "cross_cutting": {
    "note": "In every strace run the VM reads the whole SDK priv tree (about 2,800 .bl files plus native .so, precompiled.term, codegen.sources, libz3) in repeated bursts. Per run: 12-17 bursts of more than 20 files, of which 2-4 read 1,100-2,800 files each (216-358 ms for 2,772-2,818 files). Together they take 1.5-1.7 s (sweep_ms in each run) inside phases 4-7. precompiled.term is opened 8 times per run."
